      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "75 patients with postoperative peritoneal adhesions, complicated by a severe pain syndrome, were operated on during 2003-2006 yy. The preoperative use of the enzyme medication <Collagenase KK> in 28 patients allowed therefore the conduction of adequate laparoscopic adhesiolysis. There were no complications and recurrences registered at follow-up. The postoperative hospital stay averaged 3.7 days."},
